This product includes code adapted from hyper-ambient-mini
(https://github.com/tbrignonen-ai/hyper-ambient-mini), licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0. The adapted pieces are the 16 kHz WAV
framing helpers, the int16 energy measurement, and the junk-transcript
filter in src/hyper_ambient_maxi/ears/wavutil.py, taken from
app/mini_harness.py. See that file's header.

hyper-ambient (https://github.com/tbrignonen-ai/hyper-ambient) was
studied for its ears / turn / brain / mouth split and for the idea that
a local llama-server and a remote chat model share one OpenAI-compatible
client. That repository has no LICENSE file, so none of its source is
copied here.

Portions of the salience ranking, the constraint-conflict warning, the
continuity router, the lexical overlap (including its Damerau-Levenshtein
fallback), and the MCP tool names friend_context / friend_remember are
adapted from AI Friend 1.8.3, "the friend who remembers". The Origin
clone returned HTTP 403; the 1.8.3 tree used here is the attached
release archive, whose LICENSE file is the MIT License. That work is:

    Copyright 2026 AI Friend contributors
    Licensed under the MIT License.

The adapted modules are src/hyper_ambient_maxi/memory/textutil.py,
salience.py, initiative.py, router.py, and the tool schema in
mcp_server.py. Scores from the 1.8.3 context formatter are not rendered.
The write-then-read-back journal is original to this project and stays
under the Apache License, Version 2.0, as does the rest of the tree.
The MIT notice above covers only those adapted portions. No AI Friend
source files are vendored. Private install notes from that tree were
not copied.

LiquidAI LFM3-Audio-2B weights are not included. Those weights are
under the LFM Open License v1.0 and stay on the machine that already
has them.
